Theorem RL-1: RC inc emission when a value is duplicated to an Owned param while still live

  Preconditions:
    - RL-1 governs RcInc emission per Annex E §AIMS RC Emission:
      "RC inc SHALL be emitted when a value is duplicated (passed to an
      Owned param while still live)."
    - The realization rules have the common signature
      ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; RL-1 is discharged here
      against the sec-01 Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-1 consumes the converged AimsStateMap from Step 4
      (analyze_function) per Annex E §AIMS PL-2; emission runs in
      Step 5 (realize_rc_reuse, pre-merge).
    - Shipped emission sites:
        * emit_rc/forward_walk.rs::emit_terminator_rc — terminator-position
          inc emission.
        * realize/mod.rs::inject_cow_borrowed_receiver_incs (lines 406-478)
          — RcInc before a COW call whose receiver is a borrowed function
          parameter, so the runtime observes RC > 1 and takes the COW slow
          path (the extra inc is matched by the slow path's dec of the old
          buffer).
        * realize/mod.rs::realize_rc_reuse (lines 106-182) Sub-step B
          dispatches unified RC emission via emit_unified::emit_rc_unified
          (line 140), routing every inc/dec decision through
          realize/decide.rs.
    - RL-1 is gated by DP-3 (is_rc_inc_elidable, Appendix C): an inc is
      ELIDED exactly when Cardinality = Once AND Consumption is Linear or
      Affine (the value is used once, so no new owned reference is created —
      a move (Linear) transfers the existing reference, a borrow (Affine)
      reads it non-consumingly and releases it via its own RL-2 scope-exit
      dec). RL-1 emits the inc in every other duplication case (the value is
      still live afterward).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-3 (is_rc_inc_elidable) soundness is proven at
      sec-05; RL-1's emission decision consumes that predicate.

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v allocated with RC = 1 (TF-3 FRESH allocation), and
    forall duplication of v to an Owned parameter at a program point where
    v remains live afterward:

      (P1) Emission decision: RL-1 emits an RcInc for the duplication iff
           NOT is_rc_inc_elidable(state(v)) — i.e. iff NOT (Cardinality(v)
           = Once AND Consumption(v) is Linear or Affine). A single-use
           value's inc is elided because the single use creates no new owned
           reference (move transfers the sole reference; borrow releases via
           its own scope-exit dec).

      (P2) RC-count preservation (refinement of plain ARC): over v's full
           lifecycle, every reference created — the 1 from allocation plus
           every RL-1 inc — is released exactly once by a matching RcDec
           (RL-2 at the callee's last use of the Owned param, or the
           caller's last use), or by an ownership handoff. The net
           reference count returns to 0; no reference leaks and none is
           double-released.

    RL-1 refines plain ARC: plain ARC incs on EVERY duplication
    unconditionally; RL-1 emits the inc only when the value is still live
    (DP-3 elides the single-use case, move or borrow), eliminating the
    redundant inc/dec pair on a single use while preserving the same
    observable RC balance.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine via per-instruction
    RC-delta arithmetic + balance-equation witness construction (per
    the proof-checker design sec-Engine-per-Category-Inventory; the foundational-axiom policy
    sec-Per-Engine-Constructive-Proof-Shape forbids classical existence of
    a balancing witness — the witness is constructed).

    Part (P1) — emission decision (cross-check against DP-3):

      The verifier enumerates a decision grid over (Cardinality,
      Consumption) and asserts RL-1's emit-inc decision equals
      NOT dp3_inc_elidable(card, cons) on every row:
        (Once, Linear) -> elide (single-use move transfers the reference)
        (Once, Affine) -> elide (single-use borrow; own scope-exit dec balances)
        (Many, Unrestricted) -> emit (live after dup)
        (Many, Affine) -> emit (live after dup)
        (Once, Unrestricted) -> emit (re-used)
      Coverage gate: 5 decisions, each cross-checked against the
      sec-05-proven DP-3 predicate. A divergence between RL-1's emission and
      the DP-3 gate fails the proof.

    Part (P2) — RC-count preservation (balance ledger):

      A value lifecycle is modeled as an ordered sequence of RcEvents
      (Alloc / IncLiveDup / ElideIncMove / DecLastUse / TransferOut); the
      verifier computes net = (refs_created) - (refs_released) and asserts
      net = 0 for every sound lifecycle. Discharged cases:
        live_dup_owned_param_balanced — alloc, RL-1 inc on dup, callee dec,
                                          caller dec at last use -> net 0.
        moved_once_inc_elided_balanced — alloc, inc elided, ownership
                                          transfers out -> net 0.
        two_live_dups_balanced — alloc, two RL-1 incs, three decs
                                          -> net 0.

    Negative-direction witnesses (the balance check has teeth — a wrong
    emission schedule is REJECTED):
      NEG_inc_on_moved_once_leaks — RL-1 wrongly emitting an inc on a
                                          moved-once value (failing to elide)
                                          leaves an extra reference: net = +1
                                          (leak). Rejected.
      NEG_inc_without_matching_dec_leaks— an inc with no matching callee dec:
                                          net = +1 (leak). Rejected.
      Coverage gate: 5 ledger cases (3 sound + 2 negative witnesses).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl1_inc_on_live_duplication;
        per-instruction RC-delta arithmetic over the balance ledger +
        DP-3 emission-decision cross-check; emits Fail on a balance
        violation or an emission/DP-3 divergence)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row once rc_counting has discharged)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest
        RL row once rc_counting has discharged)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-1 via (P1) the inc-emission decision cross-checked against the DP-3 elision gate over a 5-row (Cardinality x Consumption) grid and (P2) the RC-count-preservation balance ledger (3 sound lifecycles + 2 negative-direction witnesses), grounded in the shipped emit_rc/forward_walk.rs + realize/mod.rs inject_cow_borrowed_receiver_incs emission sites routed through realize/decide.rs
